Subject: [PATCH] fix/bench-entry-and-host-seat: one door onto the bench; the
 host's hand is never stayed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every path onto the bench now runs through takeBenchSeat(), which AWAITS
the headshot capture before the role write, restores silently when
face_json is already on file (no re-prompt), and degrades gracefully to
the silhouette when the camera is denied.  The join_line RPC is the single
bench-role write site, inside that one function.

Host tap on a bench chip seats that person at bench count 1, 2, or 3;
the three-at-once rule survives only as the automatic curtain-up when
three sit benched with no host tap.  Host tap always wins.

New gate 12-bench-entry: AST-proves the single write site sits inside
takeBenchSeat, drives both capture paths, the silent rejoin, taps at
every bench count, and the auto-curtain — all through the real UI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
